{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check whether a list contains the given sublist or not.\nassert is_sublist([2,4,3,5,7],[3,7])==False\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef is_sublist(main_list, sub_list):\n    \"\"\"Check if sub_list appears as a contiguous sequence in main_list.\"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n    \n    for i in range(len(main_list) - len(sub_list) + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+len(sub_list)] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check whether a list contains the given sublist or not.\nassert is_sublist([2,4,3,5,7],[3,7])==False\n\"\"\"\ndef is_sublist(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"Check if sublist exists as consecutive elements in main_list.\"\"\"\n    if not sublist:\n        return True\n    \n    sublist_len = len(sublist)\n    main_len = len(main_list)\n    \n    for i in range(main_len - sublist_len + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i + sublist_len] == sublist:\n            return True\n    \n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/70", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find whether all the given tuples have equal length or not.\nassert get_equal([(11, 22, 33), (44, 55, 66)]) == True\n\"\"\"\ndef get_equal(tuples_list):\n    \"\"\"Check if all tuples in the list have equal length.\"\"\"\n    if not tuples_list:\n        return True\n    first_length = len(tuples_list[0])\n    return all(len(t) == first_length for t in tuples_list)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the number of ways to partition a set of Bell numbers.\nassert bell_number(2)==2\n\"\"\"\ndef bell_number(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the nth Bell number using dynamic programming with Stirling numbers of the second kind.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Create a 2D array to store Stirling numbers of the second kind\n    stirling = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base cases\n    stirling[0][0] = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        stirling[i][0] = 0\n        stirling[i][i] = 1\n    \n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table using recurrence relation\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, min(i, n) + 1):\n            if i > j:\n                stirling[i][j] = j * stirling[i-1][j] + stirling[i-1][j-1]\n    \n    # Bell number is the sum of all Stirling numbers S(n, k) for k = 0 to n\n    bell = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell += stirling[n][k]\n    \n    return bell"}
