{"task_id": "Mbpp/98", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to multiply all the numbers in a list and divide with the length of the list.\nassert math.isclose(multiply_num((8, 2, 3, -1, 7)), -67.2, rel_tol=0.001)\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef multiply_num(numbers):\n    \"\"\"Multiply all numbers in a list and divide by the length of the list.\"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n    \n    product = 1\n    for num in numbers:\n        product *= num\n    \n    return product / len(numbers)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the Eulerian number a(n, m).\nassert eulerian_num(3, 1) == 4\n\"\"\"\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the Eulerian number A(n,m) using the recurrence relation.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1 if m == 0 else 0\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Use dynamic programming to build the triangle\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):\n            dp[i][j] = (j + 1) * dp[i-1][j] + (i - j) * dp[i-1][j-1] if j > 0 else dp[i-1][0]\n    \n    return dp[n][m]"}
