{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times.\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string, rotations):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of numbers with odd values when rotating binary string.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(binary_string)\n    \n    for i in range(rotations):\n        rotated = binary_string[i:] + binary_string[:i]\n        decimal_value = int(rotated, 2)\n        if decimal_value % 2 == 1:\n            count += 1\n    \n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the number of numbers with an odd value when rotating a binary string the given number of times.\nassert odd_Equivalent(\"011001\",6) == 3\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string, rotations):\n    \"\"\"Returns count of odd numbers when rotating binary string given number of times.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(binary_string)\n    \n    for i in range(rotations):\n        rotated = binary_string[i % n:] + binary_string[:i % n]\n        decimal_value = int(rotated, 2)\n        if decimal_value % 2 == 1:\n            count += 1\n    \n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the common elements in given nested lists.\nassert set(common_in_nested_lists([[12, 18, 23, 25, 45], [7, 12, 18, 24, 28], [1, 5, 8, 12, 15, 16, 18]]))==set([18, 12])\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return []\n    \n    common = set(nested_lists[0])\n    for lst in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common &= set(lst)\n    \n    return list(common)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the common elements in given nested lists.\nassert set(common_in_nested_lists([[12, 18, 23, 25, 45], [7, 12, 18, 24, 28], [1, 5, 8, 12, 15, 16, 18]]))==set([18, 12])\n\"\"\"\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"Find common elements across all nested lists.\"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return []\n    \n    common = set(nested_lists[0])\n    for lst in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common &= set(lst)\n    \n    return list(common)"}
