{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that xor to an even number.\nassert find_even_pair([5, 4, 7, 2, 1]) == 4\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef find_even_pair(nums):\n    # Two numbers XOR to even if they have same parity (both odd or both even)\n    odd_count = sum(1 for num in nums if num % 2 == 1)\n    even_count = len(nums) - odd_count\n    return odd_count * (odd_count - 1) // 2 + even_count * (even_count - 1) // 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that xor to an even number.\nassert find_even_pair([5, 4, 7, 2, 1]) == 4\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef find_even_pair(nums):\n    \"\"\"Count pairs of integers that XOR to an even number.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):\n            if (nums[i] ^ nums[j]) % 2 == 0:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
