{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list of tuples and returns a dictionary mapping each unique tuple to the number of times it occurs in the list.\nassert check_occurences([(3, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (5, 2), (6, 3)] ) == {(1, 3): 2, (2, 5): 2, (3, 6): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef check_occurences(tuples_list):\n    \"\"\"Returns a dictionary mapping each unique tuple to its occurrence count.\"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for tup in tuples_list:\n        # Normalize tuple to canonical form (smaller element first)\n        canonical = tuple(sorted(tup))\n        result[canonical] = result.get(canonical, 0) + 1\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set all even bits of a given number.\nassert even_bit_set_number(10) == 10\n\"\"\"\ndef even_bit_set_number(n):\n    \"\"\"Set all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, ...) to 1 in the given number.\"\"\"\n    mask = 0x55555555  # Binary: ...01010101 (sets even bits)\n    return n | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/240", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in two lists and replaces the last element of the first list with the elements of the second list.\nassert replace_list([1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 10],[2, 4, 6, 8])==[1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 2, 4, 6, 8]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef replace_list(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Replaces the last element of list1 with all elements from list2.\"\"\"\n    if not list1:\n        return list2[:]\n    return list1[:-1] + list2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list of tuples and returns a dictionary mapping each unique tuple to the number of times it occurs in the list.\nassert check_occurences([(3, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (5, 2), (6, 3)] ) == {(1, 3): 2, (2, 5): 2, (3, 6): 1}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef check_occurences(tuples_list):\n    # Count occurrences of each tuple, treating (a,b) and (b,a) as equivalent\n    count_dict = {}\n    for tup in tuples_list:\n        # Normalize tuple by sorting to treat (a,b) same as (b,a)\n        normalized = tuple(sorted(tup))\n        count_dict[normalized] = count_dict.get(normalized, 0) + 1\n    return count_dict\n```"}
