{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the next perfect square greater than a given number.\nassert next_Perfect_Square(35) == 36\n\"\"\"\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the next perfect square greater than n.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    sqrt_n = int(math.sqrt(n))\n    if sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) ** 2\n    else:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) ** 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in positive integers m and n and finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(10, 4) == 4\n\"\"\"\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2*previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # Previous element must be <= j//2\n            for prev in range(1, j // 2 + 1):\n                dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in positive integers m and n and finds the number of possible sequences of length n, such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal to twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\nassert get_total_number_of_sequences(10, 4) == 4\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the number of valid sequences of length n with elements <= m where each element >= 2 * previous.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            # For each ending value j, sum all valid previous values\n            for prev in range(1, min(j // 2, m) + 1):\n                if 2 * prev <= j:\n                    dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][prev]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    return sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the next perfect square greater than a given number.\nassert next_Perfect_Square(35) == 36\n\"\"\"\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n):\n    \"\"\"Find the next perfect square greater than the given number.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    sqrt_n = int(math.sqrt(n))\n    if sqrt_n * sqrt_n == n:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) * (sqrt_n + 1)\n    else:\n        return (sqrt_n + 1) * (sqrt_n + 1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes an array and finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array, where a sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Calculate maximum sum increasing subsequence ending at each index\n    inc = [0] * n\n    inc[0] = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Calculate maximum sum decreasing subsequence starting at each index\n    dec = [0] * n\n    dec[n-1] = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Find maximum bitonic sum\n    max_bitonic = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic = max(max_bitonic, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n    \n    return max_bitonic"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes an array and finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array, where a sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\nassert max_sum([1, 15, 51, 45, 33, 100, 12, 18, 9]) == 194\n\"\"\"\ndef max_sum(arr):\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n    \n    # Calculate increasing subsequence sums ending at each position\n    inc = [0] * n\n    inc[0] = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Calculate decreasing subsequence sums starting from each position\n    dec = [0] * n\n    dec[n-1] = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Find maximum sum by combining increasing and decreasing parts\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n    \n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
