{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function that takes in a non-negative number and returns the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\nassert count_Primes_nums(5) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Count prime numbers less than n using Sieve of Eratosthenes.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n    \n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n    \n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i*i, n, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n    \n    return sum(is_prime)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function that takes in a non-negative number and returns the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\nassert count_Primes_nums(5) == 2\n\"\"\"\ndef count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Count prime numbers less than n.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return 0\n    \n    is_prime = [True] * n\n    is_prime[0] = is_prime[1] = False\n    \n    for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[i]:\n            for j in range(i*i, n, i):\n                is_prime[j] = False\n    \n    return sum(is_prime)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list and length n, and generates all combinations (with repetition) of the elements of the list and returns a list with a tuple for each combination.\nassert combinations_colors( [\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],1)==[('Red',), ('Green',), ('Blue',)]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef combinations_colors(colors, n):\n    \"\"\"Generate all combinations with repetition of given length.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    \n    result = []\n    for color in colors:\n        for combo in combinations_colors(colors, n - 1):\n            result.append((color,) + combo)\n    \n    return result\n```"}
