{"task_id": "Mbpp/255", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function that takes in a list and length n, and generates all combinations (with repetition) of the elements of the list and returns a list with a tuple for each combination.\nassert combinations_colors( [\"Red\",\"Green\",\"Blue\"],1)==[('Red',), ('Green',), ('Blue',)]\n\"\"\"\ndef combinations_colors(colors, n):\n    \"\"\"Generate all combinations with repetition of length n from colors list.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [()]\n    \n    result = []\n    \n    def generate_combinations(current_combo, remaining_length):\n        if remaining_length == 0:\n            result.append(tuple(current_combo))\n            return\n        \n        for color in colors:\n            current_combo.append(color)\n            generate_combinations(current_combo, remaining_length - 1)\n            current_combo.pop()\n    \n    generate_combinations([], n)\n    return result"}
