{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    \"\"\"Set the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of n.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the position of the most significant bit\n    temp = n\n    msb_pos = 0\n    while temp:\n        msb_pos += 1\n        temp >>= 1\n    \n    # Check if the bit at msb_pos is set, if not set it\n    bit_to_check = 1 << msb_pos\n    if (n & bit_to_check) == 0:\n        return n | bit_to_check\n    \n    # If msb+1 position bit is not set, set it\n    return n | (1 << msb_pos)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\nassert highest_Power_of_2(10) == 8\n\"\"\"\ndef highest_Power_of_2(n):\n    \"\"\"Find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    power = 1\n    while power * 2 <= n:\n        power *= 2\n    \n    return power"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to set the left most unset bit.\nassert set_left_most_unset_bit(10) == 14\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit and set it\n    temp = n\n    position = 0\n    \n    # Find the leftmost unset bit position\n    while temp > 0:\n        if (temp & 1) == 0:\n            leftmost_unset_pos = position\n        temp >>= 1\n        position += 1\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next bit\n    if temp == 0 and n > 0:\n        # Check if all bits in n are set\n        all_set = True\n        temp = n\n        while temp > 0:\n            if (temp & 1) == 0:\n                all_set = False\n                break\n            temp >>= 1\n        \n        if all_set:\n            return n | (1 << position)\n    \n    # Set the leftmost unset bit\n    return n | (1 << leftmost_unset_pos)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the n'th lucas number.\nassert find_lucas(9) == 76\n\"\"\"\ndef find_lucas(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the n'th Lucas number.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    a, b = 2, 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
