{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum possible by using the given equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\nassert get_max_sum(60) == 106\n\"\"\"\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def helper(num):\n        if num in memo:\n            return memo[num]\n        \n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        recursive_sum = helper(num // 2) + helper(num // 3) + helper(num // 4) + helper(num // 5)\n        result = max(recursive_sum, num)\n        memo[num] = result\n        return result\n    \n    return helper(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/394", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check if given tuple contains no duplicates.\nassert check_distinct((1, 4, 5, 6, 1, 4)) == False\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef check_distinct(tup):\n    \"\"\"Check if tuple contains no duplicates.\"\"\"\n    return len(tup) == len(set(tup))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the maximum sum possible by using the given equation f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\nassert get_max_sum(60) == 106\n\"\"\"\ndef get_max_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns maximum sum using equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n    \n    def helper(num):\n        if num in memo:\n            return memo[num]\n        \n        if num == 0:\n            return 0\n        \n        split_sum = helper(num // 2) + helper(num // 3) + helper(num // 4) + helper(num // 5)\n        result = max(split_sum, num)\n        memo[num] = result\n        return result\n    \n    return helper(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the first non-repeated character in a given string.\nassert first_non_repeating_character(\"abcabc\") == None\n\"\"\"\ndef first_non_repeating_character(s):\n    \"\"\"Find the first character that appears exactly once in the string.\"\"\"\n    char_count = {}\n    \n    # Count occurrences of each character\n    for char in s:\n        char_count[char] = char_count.get(char, 0) + 1\n    \n    # Find first character with count of 1\n    for char in s:\n        if char_count[char] == 1:\n            return char\n    \n    return None"}
