{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to sort the given array by using shell sort.\nassert shell_sort([12, 23, 4, 5, 3, 2, 12, 81, 56, 95]) == [2, 3, 4, 5, 12, 12, 23, 56, 81, 95]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sort array using shell sort algorithm with decreasing gap sequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2\n    \n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    \n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to extract the elementwise and tuples from the given two tuples.\nassert and_tuples((10, 4, 6, 9), (5, 2, 3, 3)) == (0, 0, 2, 1)\n\"\"\"\ndef and_tuples(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Extract elementwise AND operation from two tuples.\"\"\"\n    return tuple(a & b for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to sort the given array by using shell sort.\nassert shell_sort([12, 23, 4, 5, 3, 2, 12, 81, 56, 95]) == [2, 3, 4, 5, 12, 12, 23, 56, 81, 95]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef shell_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts array using shell sort algorithm with gap sequence.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    gap = n // 2\n    \n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = arr[i]\n            j = i\n            while j >= gap and arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                arr[j] = arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    \n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the directrix of a parabola.\nassert parabola_directrix(5,3,2)==-198\n\"\"\"\ndef parabola_directrix(a, h, k):\n    # For parabola (x-h)^2 = 4p(y-k), directrix is y = k - p where p = 1/(4a)\n    p = 1 / (4 * a)\n    return k - p"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/430", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the directrix of a parabola.\nassert parabola_directrix(5,3,2)==-198\n\"\"\"\ndef parabola_directrix(a, h, k):\n    \"\"\"Returns the directrix of a parabola in vertex form y = a(x-h)\u00b2 + k.\"\"\"\n    return k - 1 / (4 * a)"}
