{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to calculate the sum of perrin numbers.\nassert cal_sum(9) == 49\n\"\"\"\ndef cal_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculate sum of first n Perrin numbers.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    # First three Perrin numbers\n    p0, p1, p2 = 3, 0, 2\n    \n    if n == 1:\n        return p0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return p0 + p1\n    elif n == 3:\n        return p0 + p1 + p2\n    \n    total = p0 + p1 + p2\n    \n    # Generate remaining Perrin numbers and add to sum\n    for i in range(3, n):\n        next_perrin = p0 + p1\n        total += next_perrin\n        p0, p1, p2 = p1, p2, next_perrin\n    \n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the first adverb and their positions in a given sentence.\nassert find_adverb_position(\"clearly!! we can see the sky\")==(0, 7, 'clearly')\n\"\"\"\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence):\n    \"\"\"Find the first adverb and its position in the sentence.\"\"\"\n    import re\n    \n    # Remove punctuation and split into words\n    words = re.findall(r'\\b\\w+\\b', sentence.lower())\n    \n    # Common adverb patterns and known adverbs\n    adverb_suffixes = ['ly', 'ward', 'wise']\n    common_adverbs = {'very', 'quite', 'rather', 'too', 'so', 'how', 'when', 'where', 'why', 'here', 'there', 'now', 'then', 'always', 'never', 'often', 'sometimes', 'usually', 'quickly', 'slowly', 'well', 'badly', 'hard', 'fast', 'early', 'late', 'soon', 'again', 'already', 'still', 'yet', 'just', 'only', 'almost', 'nearly', 'quite', 'really', 'truly', 'certainly', 'probably', 'perhaps', 'maybe', 'clearly', 'obviously', 'definitely', 'absolutely', 'completely', 'entirely', 'fully', 'hardly', 'scarcely', 'barely'}\n    \n    for i, word in enumerate(words):\n        # Check if word is a known adverb or ends with common adverb suffix\n        if word in common_adverbs or any(word.endswith(suffix) for suffix in adverb_suffixes):\n            # Find the actual position in original sentence\n            start_pos = sentence.lower().find(word)\n            end_pos = start_pos + len(word)\n            return (start_pos, end_pos, word)\n    \n    return None"}
