{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\nassert tuple_intersection([(3, 4), (5, 6), (9, 10), (4, 5)] , [(5, 4), (3, 4), (6, 5), (9, 11)]) == {(4, 5), (3, 4), (5, 6)}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Find intersection of tuples regardless of element order.\"\"\"\n    def normalize_tuple(t):\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n    \n    set1 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    set2 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n    \n    return set1 & set2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\nassert tuple_intersection([(3, 4), (5, 6), (9, 10), (4, 5)] , [(5, 4), (3, 4), (6, 5), (9, 11)]) == {(4, 5), (3, 4), (5, 6)}\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef tuple_intersection(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Find intersection of tuples considering order-independent matching.\"\"\"\n    def normalize_tuple(t):\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n    \n    set1 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1}\n    set2 = {normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n    \n    intersection = set1 & set2\n    \n    result = set()\n    for t in list1:\n        if normalize_tuple(t) in intersection:\n            result.add(t)\n    \n    return result\n```"}
