{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to convert polar coordinates to rectangular coordinates.\nassert polar_rect(3,4)==((5.0, 0.9272952180016122), (-2+2.4492935982947064e-16j))\n\"\"\"\ndef polar_rect(r, theta):\n    \"\"\"Convert polar coordinates (r, theta) to rectangular coordinates and complex form.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    x = r * math.cos(theta)\n    y = r * math.sin(theta)\n    magnitude = math.sqrt(x**2 + y**2)\n    angle = math.atan2(y, x)\n    complex_form = complex(x, y)\n    return ((magnitude, angle), complex_form)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/591", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to interchange the first and last elements in a list.\nassert swap_List([12, 35, 9, 56, 24]) == [24, 35, 9, 56, 12]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef swap_List(lst):\n    \"\"\"Interchange the first and last elements in a list.\"\"\"\n    if len(lst) <= 1:\n        return lst\n    lst[0], lst[-1] = lst[-1], lst[0]\n    return lst\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/590", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to convert polar coordinates to rectangular coordinates.\nassert polar_rect(3,4)==((5.0, 0.9272952180016122), (-2+2.4492935982947064e-16j))\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef polar_rect(x, y):\n    \"\"\"Convert rectangular coordinates to polar, then return both polar and complex rectangular form.\"\"\"\n    import math\n    r = math.sqrt(x*x + y*y)\n    theta = math.atan2(y, x)\n    complex_form = complex(x, y)\n    return ((r, theta), complex_form)\n```"}
