{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to get all lucid numbers smaller than or equal to a given integer.\nassert get_ludic(10) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all Ludic numbers less than or equal to n.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # First number is always Ludic\n        first = numbers.pop(0)\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        if first == 1:\n            continue\n            \n        # Remove every first-th number from remaining list\n        new_numbers = []\n        for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n            if (i + 1) % first != 0:\n                new_numbers.append(num)\n        numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic\n```"}
