{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check if the given array represents min heap or not. \nassert check_min_heap([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]) == True\n\"\"\"\ndef check_min_heap(arr):\n    \"\"\"Check if array represents a min heap where parent <= children.\"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n    \n    for i in range(len(arr)):\n        left_child = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child = 2 * i + 2\n        \n        if left_child < len(arr) and arr[i] > arr[left_child]:\n            return False\n        if right_child < len(arr) and arr[i] > arr[right_child]:\n            return False\n    \n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to find the nth jacobsthal number.  0, 1, 1, 3, 5, 11, 21, 43, 85, 171, 341, 683, 1365, 2731, ...\nassert jacobsthal_num(5) == 11\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n):\n    \"\"\"Return the nth Jacobsthal number using the recurrence relation J(n) = J(n-1) + 2*J(n-2).\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    a, b = 0, 1\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, b + 2 * a\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWe say that an element is common for lists l1, l2, l3 if it appears in all three lists under the same index. Write a function to find common elements from three lists. The function should return a list.\nassert extract_index_list([1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7])==[1, 7]\n\"\"\"\ndef extract_index_list(l1, l2, l3):\n    \"\"\"Find elements that appear at the same index in all three lists.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    min_len = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    for i in range(min_len):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            result.append(l1[i])\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a function to check if the given array represents min heap or not. \nassert check_min_heap([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]) == True\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef check_min_heap(arr):\n    \"\"\"Check if array represents a min heap where parent <= children.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child = 2 * i + 2\n        \n        if left_child < n and arr[i] > arr[left_child]:\n            return False\n        if right_child < n and arr[i] > arr[right_child]:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/754", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWe say that an element is common for lists l1, l2, l3 if it appears in all three lists under the same index. Write a function to find common elements from three lists. The function should return a list.\nassert extract_index_list([1, 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7],[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7])==[1, 7]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef extract_index_list(l1, l2, l3):\n    \"\"\"Returns elements that appear at the same index in all three lists.\"\"\"\n    common_elements = []\n    min_length = min(len(l1), len(l2), len(l3))\n    \n    for i in range(min_length):\n        if l1[i] == l2[i] == l3[i]:\n            common_elements.append(l1[i])\n    \n    return common_elements\n```"}
