{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to count the number of pairs whose sum is equal to \u2018sum\u2019. The funtion gets as input a list of numbers and the sum,\nassert get_pairs_count([1,1,1,1],2) == 6\n\"\"\"\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers, target_sum):\n    \"\"\"Count pairs in the list whose sum equals target_sum.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(len(numbers)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(numbers)):\n            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == target_sum:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the sum of fourth power of first n odd natural numbers.\nassert odd_num_sum(2) == 82\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_num_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns the sum of fourth power of first n odd natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        odd_num = 2 * i + 1\n        total += odd_num ** 4\n    return total"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/769", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to get the difference between two lists.\nassert (Diff([10, 15, 20, 25, 30, 35, 40], [25, 40, 35])) == [10, 20, 30, 15]\n\"\"\"\n```python\ndef Diff(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"Returns elements in list1 that are not in list2, preserving original order.\"\"\"\n    return [item for item in list1 if item not in list2]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/770", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the sum of fourth power of first n odd natural numbers.\nassert odd_num_sum(2) == 82\n\"\"\"\ndef odd_num_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculate the sum of fourth power of first n odd natural numbers.\"\"\"\n    return sum((2*i - 1)**4 for i in range(1, n + 1))"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to count the number of pairs whose sum is equal to \u2018sum\u2019. The funtion gets as input a list of numbers and the sum,\nassert get_pairs_count([1,1,1,1],2) == 6\n\"\"\"\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers, target_sum):\n    \"\"\"Count pairs of numbers that sum to target_sum.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(len(numbers)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(numbers)):\n            if numbers[i] + numbers[j] == target_sum:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
